{
  "_comment": [
    "The coord-core program's step-4 move set: the 68 modules plan 3962 T1 names, with the",
    "destination layer each one moves to. Committed by plan 4061 (step 4a) so that step 4's work",
    "list is DATA rather than something a later session re-derives by hand, per operator decision 3",
    "of 2026-09-19 ('the closure remainder is named in 4061's table rather than discovered",
    "mid-diff'). scripts/coord/module-graph.mjs closes over these seeds to produce the split list,",
    "and module-graph.test.mjs asserts plan 4061's acceptance against that same closure.",
    "Source of truth for the classification is plan 3962 § T1; this file is its machine-readable",
    "projection and must be regenerated, not hand-edited, if that table changes.",
    "ONE row diverges from 3962 § T1's literal wording, and by that table's own instruction:",
    "it listed 'cloud-routine-prompt-lib (until step 6 splits it)' as BLOCKED. Step 6 (plan 3964",
    "T2) performed that split, so the row now names its surviving project-side half,",
    "scripts/project/cloud-routine-specs.mjs, and is classed SPLIT. The generic half went to",
    "scripts/coord/routine-prompt-engine.mjs and needs no row of its own: it is already at a core",
    "destination and the closure reaches it through the specs module that imports it.",
    "FIVE MORE rows diverge from 3962 § T1, by plan 4096 T6 (2026-09-22): the wiki family",
    "(wiki-fold, wiki-log-lint, wiki-size-lint, wiki-updated-merge-driver, wiki-coverage-sweep)",
    "was classed scripts/project/ there and is classed scripts/coord/ here. Reason: the coord kit",
    "ships the wiki surface as a GENERIC coord feature — coord-kit-manifest.json carries wiki-commit",
    "in commands, docs/coord in dirs and a wikiScaffold for wiki/{index,hot,log}.md — so a",
    "project-side wiki family would leave wiki-commit permanently blocked at the kit closure gate,",
    "which is the defect plan 4096 exists to close. None of the five names a vetapp concept; they",
    "are frontmatter parsing, a size budget, a log lint, a merge driver and a coverage sweep."
  ],
